      "content": "**What**: SDD proposal for `plugin-doc-site` — an Astro + Starlight + GSAP documentation site for the agent007 plugin, statically deployed to Vercel. Six scroll sections (hero with ASCII→ecosystem-tree cinematic, orchestrator pipeline loop, skills/agents/hooks grid, install terminal, roadmap timeline, \"Watch it think\" client-side mock).\n\n**Why**: External devs are asking how the plugin works (issues + direct questions). Current docs describe but don't transmit craft. Post-v7.2 momentum window. Goal: 30-second landing convinces tooling-savvy devs \"this is serious engineering\" without reading. Success is subjective (author proud to share + 1 of 3 trusted devs reacts positively).\n\n**Where**:\n- Proposal file: `.sdlc/specs/plugin-doc-site/proposal.md`\n- Inputs read: `.sdlc/prds/2026-05-plugin-doc-site.md`, `.sdlc/specs/plugin-doc-site/DECISIONS.md`\n- Target site location: TBD in sdd-design (likely `doc/`, but filesystem check shows directory does not exist — CONTEXT.md reference is stale)\n\n**Scope IN**: Astro+Starlight+GSAP stack, 6 locked sections, graphite/mono/terminal-green palette, privacy-friendly analytics + cookie banner, WCAG AA, LCP\u003c2s mobile, JS-off graceful degradation.\n\n**Scope OUT**: Docusaurus-style ref docs, full-text search, blog, sponsor buttons, auto API docs, vs-competitors tables, author bio, server functions.\n\n**Slicing**: spec (per-section behavioral contract) → design (resolves 4 deferred questions + doc/ disposition + Vercel setup) → tasks (grouped by section for visual checkpoints, section 6 isolated as cut-candidate) → apply → verify (acceptance criteria + Lighthouse + cross-browser ASCII + JS-off smoke) → archive.\n\n**Learned / Risks surfaced beyond PRD+DECISIONS**:\n- R1: `doc/` Next.js dir referenced in CONTEXT.md does NOT exist on disk — sdd-design must confirm canonical project path\n- R2: Monorepo vs separate repo — default monorepo subdir, Vercel root-directory config\n- R3: No Vercel project conf