      "title": "Triki SDD v1.0 — full canonical spec for Fase 0",
      "content": "Full canonical spec from logic_triki_SDD_v1.docx (Nivel 1, v1.0). This is the source of truth — supersedes any earlier exploration assumptions.\n\n## Vision\nLogic-Triki is an educational programming game. Player writes code to control X on a 3×3 tic-tac-toe board against an optimal minimax bot. The board is the world; the code is the player.\n\n## Phase scope split\n- **Fase 0** (this proposal): Engine + Bot + API + edge cases. Pure JS, no visual, no transpiler, single-language (raw JS callback).\n- **Fase 1**: Three.js render\n- **Fase 2**: CodeMirror editor + reflexes\n- **Fase 3**: Pseudocode/Python/C++ transpilers\n\n## API CONTRACT (canonical — sec 3 of SDD)\n\n### Read functions (5) — all global\n| Function | Returns | Behavior |\n|---|---|---|\n| `celda(fila, col)` | string | \"X\", \"O\" or \"\". Range 0-2. |\n| `celda_libre(fila, col)` | boolean | celda(f,c) === \"\" |\n| `bot_jugó_en(fila, col)` | boolean | true if cell currently has bot's piece (NOT just last move) |\n| `yo_jugué_en(fila, col)` | boolean | true if cell currently has player's piece |\n| `última_jugada_bot()` | [fila,col] | coords of bot's last move. Returns [-1,-1] on turn 0 |\n\n### Read-only variables (3) — all global\n| Variable | Type | Value |\n|---|---|---|\n| `turno` | number | 0..4 (player has max 5 moves) |\n| `mi_símbolo` | string | always \"X\" |\n| `bot_símbolo` | string | always \"O\" |\n\n### Action (1)\n- `jugar(fila, col)` — void. Places X. ONE call per turn. Invalid coords or occupied cell → descriptive error. THIS IS THE ONLY WAY TO ACT.\n\n### Contract rules\n- Player is always X, always first\n- Engine validates every call\n- Errors NEVER crash the game — they pause execution with a fix suggestion\n\n## BOT (sec 4)\n\nMinimax perfecto, +10/0/-10 scoring. Tic-tac-toe has ≤362,880 states — full eval is microseconds. NO memoization needed, NO alpha-beta needed (overkill).\n\n### Decision priority (sec 4.2 — 8 priorities in strict order)\n1. Win now (take winning move)\n2. Block opponent's immediate win\n3. Create fork (two simultaneous threats)\n4. Prevent opponent fork\n5. Take center\n6. Take corner opposite to opponent\n7. Take any corner\n8. Take any side\n\nNote: pure minimax should produce these behaviors as a side-effect of optimal play, but the SDD enumerates them. Implementation strategy: implement minimax first, then write tests that verify each priority emerges. If a priority is NOT honored by pure minimax (rare — e.g., when multiple moves tie), use the priority list as tiebreaker.\n\n## EDGE CASES (sec 7 — 10 cases that MUST be handled)\n\n### Player code errors (7.1)\n1. Code ends without calling `jugar()` → pause + msg + lose turn\n2. `jugar()` called twice → first valid, second ignored with warning, continue\n3. Cell already occupied → pause + cell shakes\n4. Infinite while → cut at 50 iterations + pause\n5. Coord out of 0-2 → pause + show actual value\n6. Variable uninitialized → pause + suggest declaration\n7. Turn not covered (no branch matched) → pause + suggest default `sino`\n8. `última_jugada_bot()` on turn 0 → returns [-1,-1] + warning if used to play\n\n### Board state (7.2)\n9. Board full / tie → engine forces last valid move, declares tie\n10. Win without intention → normal win + pedagogical hint\n\nEach error returns: message + suggested fix + reflex color (red=pause, yellow=warning).\nEngine NEVER crashes. Errors are pedagogical events, not failures.\n\n## STACK (sec 8) — for context only\n- Three.js r160 (Fase 1)\n- CodeMirror 6 (Fase 2)\n- Vite (Fase 1+)\n- Transpiler propio (Fase 3)\n- Pyodide WASM for real Python (Fase 3)\n- File structure: src/board.js, src/editor.js, src/engine.js, src/bot.js, src/transpiler.js, src/sandbox.js, src/api.js\n\n## FILE STRUCTURE (sec 8.1)\n```\nlogic-triki/\n├── index.html\n├── src/\n│   ├── board.js        ← Three.js (Fase 1)\n│   ├── editor.js       ← CodeMirror (Fase 2)\n│   ├── engine.js       ← game logic, validation (Fase 0)\n│   ├── bot.js          ← Minimax (Fase 0)\n│   ├── transpiler.js   ← pseudo/Python → JS (Fase 3)\n│   ├── sandbox.js      ← runs player code with limits (Fase 0/2)\n│   └── api.js          ← celda(), jugar(), etc. (Fase 0)\n└── vite.config.js\n```\n\nNote: Fase 0 only needs `engine.js`, `bot.js`, `api.js`, and a minimal `sandbox.js` (to set up globals before invoking player callback).\n\n## OUT OF SCOPE for Fase 0\n- Three.js / any visual\n- CodeMirror / editor\n- Transpiler (pseudocode / Python / C++)\n- Pyodide\n- Reflex system (visual line coloring)\n- Language selection screen\n- Scoring system (sec 10)\n- Sandbox iteration counter visualization\n- Saved code / persistence\n\n## DECISIONS LOCKED FROM SDD (override earlier exploration)\n1. `jugar()` is CALLED as side-effect inside player code (NOT returned)\n2. API uses GLOBALS only (not state methods)\n3. `bot_jugó_en()` = \"bot has piece here now\" (NOT \"last move only\")\n4. Coordinates are 0-indexed (0..2)\n5. Player is X, always first, max 5 turns\n6. Errors pause execution, never crash",
