      "content": "# Logic-Triki SDD v1.0 — Canonical Source Spec\n\n**Nivel 1 · Versión 1.0 · Completo**\n**Tipo**: System Design Document — game design source of truth\n**Concept**: Educational programming game based on Tic-Tac-Toe\n**Languages exposed to player**: Pseudocode · Python · C++\n**Stack**: Three.js · CodeMirror 6 · Vite\n\n## Vision\nPlayer writes real code to control an X piece on a tic-tac-toe board. Engine executes that code turn by turn, animating decisions on a 2D board.\n- Loop: Player writes → engine executes → board reacts → player iterates.\n- Goal: teach algorithmic thinking (decompose into conditions, state, actions). Not to win tic-tac-toe.\n\n## Level 1 — Available blocks (ONLY these)\n- `if / else if / else` — decisions on board state, chainable\n- `while` — iterate rows/cols searching cells\n- Variables — store state between lines (numbers, strings 'X'/'O'/'', booleans)\n- NO user-defined functions, NO lists, NO for loops (locked, visible but not usable)\n\n## 4 levels of logical freedom (with only if/while/vars)\n1. **Fixed opening** — uses `turno` variable to play predefined positions. No board reading.\n2. **Reactive defense** — uses `bot_jugó_en()` to map each bot play to a response.\n3. **Search with while** — `while` to traverse rows/cols finding first free cell.\n4. **Full automation** — boolean vars + while + if to handle attack and defense same turn.\n\n## API Contract (NEVER changes between languages, only syntax)\n\n### 3.1 Board read functions (5 total)\n| Function | Returns | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `celda(fila, col)` | string | \"X\" / \"O\" / \"\" — fila,col in 0..2 |\n| `celda_libre(fila, col)` | bool | True if empty. Equivalent to `celda(f,c) == \"\"` |\n| `bot_jugó_en(fila, col)` | bool | True if bot HAS its piece there. Essential for reactive defense. |\n| `yo_jugué_en(fila, col)` | bool | True if player has piece there |\n| `última_jugada_bot()` | [fila,col] | Coords of bot's last move. Returns [-1,-1] on turn 0. |\n\n### 3.2 Read-only state variables (3 total, globals)\n| Var | Type | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| `turno` | number | 0,1,2,3,4. Player X moves max 5 times. |\n| `mi_símbolo` | string | Always \"X\" |\n| `bot_símbolo` | string | Always \"O\" |\n\n### 3.3 Action (only way to act)\n`jugar(fila, col)` → void. Places X at (fila,col). Only callable ONCE per turn. If occupied or out of range → descriptive error.\n\n## 4. Internal Bot — Minimax\n- Perfect minimax: never loses. Player perfect → tie. Player imperfect → bot wins.\n- 9! = 362,880 max states. Evaluated in microseconds.\n\n### 4.1 Score\n- Bot wins: +10 (maximize)\n- Tie: 0 (neutral)\n- Player wins: -10 (minimize)\n\n### 4.2 Decision priority (strict order — verify minimax naturally produces this)\n1. Can I win now? → take it\n2. Player wins next turn? → block. If 2 threats, block most urgent.\n3. Can I create a fork? → play cell that creates 2 simultaneous threats\n4. Player can fork? → prevent by playing on cell that eliminates that possibility\n5. Center free → take it (4 winning lines)\n6. Corner opposite to player's corner → take it\n7. Any free corner → corners participate in more winning lines\n8. Any free side → last resort, bot rarely reaches here\n\n## 6. Reflex system (visual execution)\nEach line gets a visual reflex while executing. Color layer BEHIND text, never on top.\n\n### 6.1 Four states\n- 🟢 Green — executed OK. `rgba(green, 6%)` bg, 2.5px left border. Persists until restart.\n- 🟡 Yellow — executing now. Pulse animation on left border. Duration = delay.\n- 🔴 Red — error, paused. `rgba(red, 10%)` bg, tooltip with fix. Execution pauses but doesn't end.\n- ⬜ Gray — pending. Reduced text opacity.\n\n### 6.2 Editor ↔ board sync\n- `variable = value` → vars panel highlights row yellow, shows new value\n- `si bot_jugó_en(f,c)` → cell (f,c) blinks blue (being evaluated)\n- `jugar(f,c)` → X appears with scale 0→1 in 250ms. Editor cursor waits.\n- `jugar()` error → cell shakes, red flash on grid border, red reflex on line\n\n### 6.3 Configurable speed\n- Slow 800ms / Normal 400ms (default) / Fast 150ms / Instant 0ms\n\n## 7. Edge cases (engine NEVER breaks)\nEach error produces: red reflex, tooltip with description + suggested fix, execution pause.\n\n### 7.1 Player code edge cases (8)\n1. Code ends without `jugar()` → \"Tu código no llamó jugar().\" Fix: agregá un sino con jugada alternativa.\n2. `jugar()` called twice → \"Ya jugaste este turno.\" Fix: usá if/else para elegir una sola jugada.\n3. Cell already occupied → \"La celda (f,c) tiene una ficha.\" Fix: usá celda_libre() antes de jugar.\n4. Infinite while → \"Loop infinito detectado (50+ iter).\" Fix: agregá incremento dentro del while.\n5. Coord out of 0-2 → \"fila = 3 está fuera del tablero.\" [shows real value]. Fix: revisá el cálculo.\n6. Uninitialized variable → \"mi_col no existe en este turno. Se definía dentro de un si que no se ejecutó.\" Fix: declará antes del si.\n7. Turn not covered → \"Tu código no tiene caso para turno=2.\" Fix: agregá un sino final.\n8. `última_jugada_bot()` on turn 0 → \"Bot aún no jugó. Devuelve [-1,-1].\" Fix: verificá turno \u003e 0.\n\n### 7.2 Board state edge cases (2)\n9. Board full — tie → motor fuerza última jugada válida y declara empate. NOT player error.\n10. Victory without intent → \"Ganaste, pero tu código no detectó la victoria activamente.\" Pedagogical hint.\n\n### 7.3 System response table\n| Edge case | Engine response | Continues? |\n|---|---|---|\n| No jugar() | Red reflex + msg + turn lost | Pause |\n| jugar() twice | First valid, second ignored with warning | Continue |\n| Cell occupied | Red reflex + cell shakes | Pause |\n| Infinite while | Cut at 50 iter + yellow blink | Pause |\n| Coord out of range | Red reflex + real value shown | Pause |\n| Uninit variable | Red reflex + suggest declaration spot | Pause |\n| Turn not covered | Yellow warning + suggest final sino | Pause |\n| última_jugada_bot() turn 0 | Returns [-1,-1] + warning if used to play | Pause |\n| Board full | Force last move, declare tie | Continue |\n| Victory unintended | Normal victory + pedagogical hint | Victory |\n\n## 8. Stack\n- Render 2D: Three.js r160 (board, pieces, scale/shake animations, winning line)\n- Editor: CodeMirror 6 (syntax highlight, per-line reflexes, API autocomplete)\n- Bundler: Vite (fast build, hot reload, native ES modules)\n- L1 execution: own JS transpiler (pseudocode/Python → JS in browser. No backend.)\n- Real Python: Pyodide WASM (no server, no Docker)\n- Layout: HTML + CSS overlay on Three.js canvas (no iframes)\n\n### 8.1 File structure (canonical)\n```\nlogic-triki/\n├── index.html\n├── src/\n│   ├── board.js        ← Three.js: board, pieces, animations\n│   ├── editor.js       ← CodeMirror: editor, per-line reflexes\n│   ├── engine.js       ← game logic, move validation\n│   ├── bot.js          ← Minimax bot\n│   ├── transpiler.js   ← pseudo/Python → executable JS\n│   ├── sandbox.js      ← runs player code with limits\n│   └── api.js          ← contract functions: celda(), jugar(), etc.\n└── vite.config.js\n```\n\n## 9. Full session flow\n1. Open → language selection screen (pseudocode/Python/C++)\n2. Choose language → editor with empty template + API reference in right panel\n3. Player writes logic → syntax highlight, autocomplete suggests API functions\n4. Press ▶ Execute → yellow cursor moves line by line, board animates plays\n5a. No errors → all lines green, full match plays to win/lose/tie\n5b. Error → red reflex on line, tooltip with description + fix, paused\n6. See result + score (Victory/Tie/Defeat with breakdown)\n7. Iterate code → modify and re-run, board auto-resets\n\n## 10. Scoring\n| Metric | Weight | Description |\n|---|---|---|\n| W/T/L | 50% | Win 50pts / Tie 20pts / Loss 0pts |\n| Turn efficiency | 20% | Win turn 3 \u003e win turn 5 |\n| CPU time per turn | 15% | More efficient algos get bonus |\n| Zero runtime errors | 10% | If code ran without error pauses |\n| Active victory detection | 5% bonus | Player explicitly called jugar() on winning cell |\n\n## CANONICAL RESOLUTIONS (from full SDD, for Fase 0)\n- `next_move` contract → player code CALLS `jugar()` as side-effect. Engine sets up globals, runs player code, detects `jugar()` call, applies move.\n- API scope → all functions and vars are GLOBALS during player code execution.\n- `bot_jugó_en(f,c)` → returns true if cell has bot's piece (state query). NOT redundant with `celda()` because `última_jugada_bot()` exists separately for \"most recent\" semantics.\n- Player is always X, always moves first, max 5 turns.\n- Bot must implement minimax with verification that section 4.2 priorities emerge naturally (or add tiebreakers if not).",
