      "content": "# Triki Engine — Fase 0 Specification\n\n**Change**: `triki-engine`\n**Phase**: Fase 0 — pure JS engine\n**Artifact store**: engram\n**Source of truth**: Logic-Triki SDD v1.0 (obs #13) + Proposal (obs #14)\n\n---\n\n## 1. Entry Point\n\n### Requirement: runGame signature\n\nThe engine MUST export a single named function `runGame(playerFn, options?)` from `src/index.js`.\n\n**`playerFn`**: `(state) =\u003e void`. Called once per player turn. The engine installs globals on `globalThis` before calling it and removes them after it returns. `playerFn` communicates its move exclusively via the side-effect of calling `jugar()`.\n\n**`options`** (all optional):\n| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `maxTurnMs` | number | 100 | Wall-clock timeout per player turn (ms). Triggers `ERR_INFINITE_LOOP`. |\n\n**Return shape** — all four keys MUST be present on every return:\n| Field | Type | Description |\n|-------|------|-------------|\n| `winner` | `'X' \\| 'O' \\| 'tie'` | Match result |\n| `turns` | number | Total moves played (player + bot combined, 0..9) |\n| `history` | `Array\u003cHistoryEntry\u003e` | Ordered chronologically, one entry per move |\n| `errors` | `Array\u003cTrikiError\u003e` | All errors raised during execution; empty array if none |\n\n**`HistoryEntry` shape**:\n```\n{ turn: number, player: 'X' | 'O', move: [fila, col] }\n```\n`turn` is the player-turn index (0..4). Bot moves share the player-turn index of the turn they follow.\n\n#### Scenario: Normal complete game\n\n- GIVEN a valid `playerFn` that always calls `jugar(1,1)` on turn 0 then optimal moves\n- WHEN `runGame(playerFn)` is called\n- THEN the return object contains `winner`, `turns`, `history`, and `errors`\n- AND `history` entries are ordered chronologically with correct `player` fields\n\n#### Scenario: No options provided\n\n- GIVEN `runGame(playerFn)` called without second argument\n- WHEN the engine runs\n- THEN `maxTurnMs` defaults to 100ms and the game completes normally\n\n---\n\n## 2. Player-Facing Globals\n\n### Requirement: Global API surface\n\nThe engine MUST install exactly these identifiers on `globalThis` before each `playerFn()` call and MUST delete them after the call returns (whether normally or via thrown error).\n\n| Global | Signature | Returns | Out-of-range behavior | Pre-runGame behavior |\n|--------|-----------|---------|----------------------|----------------------|\n| `celda(fila, col)` | `(number, number) =\u003e 'X' \\| 'O' \\| ''` | Cell content | Throws `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` | Throws `ReferenceError` (not installed) |\n| `celda_libre(fila, col)` | `(number, number) =\u003e boolean` | `true` if cell is `''` | Throws `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` | Throws `ReferenceError` |\n| `bot_jugó_en(fila, col)` | `(number, number) =\u003e boolean` | `true` if bot's piece occupies cell | Throws `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` | Throws `ReferenceError` |\n| `yo_jugué_en(fila, col)` | `(number, number) =\u003e boolean` | `true` if player's piece occupies cell | Throws `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` | Throws `ReferenceError` |\n| `última_jugada_bot()` | `() =\u003e [number, number]` | Bot's last move coords, or `[-1,-1]` on turn 0 | N/A | Throws `ReferenceError` |\n| `jugar(fila, col)` | `(number, number) =\u003e void` | void | Throws `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` | Throws `ReferenceError` |\n| `turno` | read-only `number` | Current player-turn index (0..4) | N/A | Not defined |\n| `mi_símbolo` | read-only `string` | Always `'X'` | N/A | Not defined |\n| `bot_símbolo` | read-only `string` | Always `'O'` | N/A | Not defined |\n\n**`fila` and `col` valid range**: integers 0..2 (inclusive). Any other value (including floats, strings, `null`, `undefined`, `NaN`) triggers `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE`.\n\n**`jugar()` idempotency rule**: The FIRST call per turn registers the move and applies it. A SECOND call within the same turn throws `ERR_JUGAR_TWICE` AND the second call is silently ignored — the first move stands. The game CONTINUES (does not terminate).\n\n**`última_jugada_bot()` on turn 0**: MUST return `[-1, -1]` without throwing. No error is raised at read time. If the returned value is subsequently passed to `jugar()`, `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` is thrown because -1 is outside 0..2.\n\n#### Scenario: Globals absent outside runGame\n\n- GIVEN `runGame` has not been called (or has already returned)\n- WHEN player code calls `celda(0,0)` directly\n- THEN a native `ReferenceError` is thrown (engine does NOT install globals outside of a turn)\n\n#### Scenario: Globals torn down after error\n\n- GIVEN a `playerFn` that throws `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE`\n- WHEN the engine catches the error\n- THEN all globals are removed from `globalThis` before the engine continues to the next turn\n\n#### Scenario: turno is read-only\n\n- GIVEN `playerFn` attempts `turno = 99`\n- WHEN the assignment executes\n- THEN the value of `turno` remains unchanged (strict-mode assignment to non-writable property fails silently in sloppy mode; engine MUST install it as a non-configurable, non-writable property)\n\n---\n\n## 3. Error Contract\n\n### Requirement: Structured errors\n\nThe engine MUST throw instances of `TrikiError` for all engine-detected edge cases. `TrikiError` MUST carry: `{ code, message, fix, turn? }`. `code` is the stable string identifier; `message` and `fix` are Spanish, end-user readable.\n\n| # | Code | Message (ES) | Fix (ES) | Precondition | Engine response |\n|---|------|-------------|---------|-------------|----------------|\n| 1 | `ERR_NO_JUGAR` | \"Tu código no llamó jugar().\" | \"Agregá un sino con una jugada alternativa.\" | `playerFn` returns without having called `jugar()` | Turn lost; game CONTINUES |\n| 2 | `ERR_JUGAR_TWICE` | \"Ya jugaste este turno.\" | \"Usá if/else para elegir una sola jugada.\" | `jugar()` called a second time within the same turn | Second call ignored; game CONTINUES |\n| 3 | `ERR_CELL_OCCUPIED` | \"La celda ({f},{c}) ya tiene una ficha.\" | \"Usá celda_libre() antes de jugar.\" | `jugar(f,c)` called on a cell that already has a piece | Turn lost; game CONTINUES |\n| 4 | `ERR_INFINITE_LOOP` | \"Loop infinito detectado (tiempo excedido).\" | \"Agregá un incremento o condición de salida en el while.\" | `playerFn` exceeds `maxTurnMs` wall-clock limit | Turn lost; game CONTINUES |\n| 5 | `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` | \"La coordenada {axis}={val} está fuera del tablero (0-2).\" | \"Revisá el cálculo de {axis}.\" | Any coord arg not in integer range 0..2 | Turn lost; game CONTINUES |\n| 6 | `ERR_UNINIT_VAR` | (Surfaced as native ReferenceError message) | \"Declarar la variable antes del bloque si/mientras.\" | Player code references an undefined JS variable | Native ReferenceError propagates; engine catches, logs to `errors`, turn lost; CONTINUES |\n| 7 | `ERR_TURN_NOT_COVERED` | \"Tu código no tiene caso para turno={n}.\" | \"Agregá un sino final para manejar todos los turnos.\" | Detectable only when `jugar()` was not called AND no explicit error thrown — same observable symptom as `ERR_NO_JUGAR` in Fase 0 | Fase 0: treated identically to `ERR_NO_JUGAR`; full detection deferred to Fase 3 transpiler |\n| 8 | `ERR_UNUSED_TURN0_LASTMOVE` | \"Bot aún no jugó. última_jugada_bot() devuelve [-1,-1].\" | \"Verificá turno \u003e 0 antes de usar última_jugada_bot().\" | `jugar(-1, -1)` called (value read from `última_jugada_bot()` on turn 0 and passed through) | `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` is thrown first (since -1 is out of range); this code is used as a hint in the error's `fix` field to identify the root cause |\n| 9 | `ERR_BOARD_FULL_TIE` | N/A — not an error | N/A | All 9 cells filled with no winner | Engine declares tie; `winner: 'tie'`; game ENDS normally (no error added to `errors`) |\n| 10 | `WARN_UNINTENDED_VICTORY` | \"Ganaste, pero tu código no detectó la victoria activamente.\" | N/A — pedagogical hint | Player wins but their last `jugar()` call was on a cell that was not part of any explicit win-checking logic (heuristic: no `celda()` or `yo_jugué_en()` read before the winning `jugar()`) | Normal victory; `winner: 'X'`; hint flag `{ code: 'WARN_UNINTENDED_VICTORY', ... }` added to `errors` (non-fatal) |\n\n**Error severity split**: Codes 1–8 add a `TrikiError` to `errors[]`. Code 9 produces no error entry. Code 10 produces a warning entry (non-fatal, game does not pause).\n\n**Note on ERR_TURN_NOT_COVERED in Fase 0**: The observable behavior in raw JS is identical to `ERR_NO_JUGAR` — `jugar()` was not called. The engine MUST use code `ERR_NO_JUGAR` in Fase 0 for both cases. `ERR_TURN_NOT_COVERED` is reserved for Fase 3 when the transpiler can inspect structure.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Bot Behavior\n\n### Requirement: Minimax bot\n\nThe bot MUST implement minimax with depth bonus scoring:\n- Bot wins: `+10 - depth` (prefer faster wins)\n- Tie: `0`\n- Player wins: `-10 + depth` (prefer slower losses)\n\nThe bot MUST select moves from a **sorted move list** (row-major order: [0,0],[0,1],[0,2],[1,0]...) to guarantee determinism when scores are equal.\n\nThe bot MUST satisfy all 8 priority behaviors from SDD §4.2 on their canonical board configurations. If minimax with depth bonus does not naturally produce priorities 6 (opposite corner) or 8 (any free side), an explicit preference table MUST be applied as a tiebreaker among equal-score moves.\n\n**8 testable priority scenarios** — given these board states, the bot's next move MUST be:\n\n| Priority | Board state | Expected bot move |\n|----------|-------------|-------------------|\n| 1 — Win now | Bot has two in a row with third cell free | Third cell of that row |\n| 2 — Block | Player has two in a row with third cell free | Third cell of that row |\n| 3 — Fork | Bot can create two simultaneous threats | The forking cell |\n| 4 — Block fork | Player can fork on next move | The cell that eliminates the fork |\n| 5 — Center | Board empty | [1,1] |\n| 6 — Opposite corner | Player played corner; opposite corner free | Opposite corner |\n| 7 — Any corner | Center taken, no corner threat | A corner cell |\n| 8 — Any side | All above not applicable | A side cell ([0,1],[1,0],[1,2],[2,1]) |\n\n#### Scenario: Bot never loses\n\n- GIVEN 100 games where player moves are random-legal\n- WHEN `runGame` completes each game\n- THEN `winner` is `'X'` or `'tie'` in all 100 games — never `'O'`\n\n#### Scenario: Perfect player forces tie\n\n- GIVEN a `playerFn` implementing optimal play\n- WHEN `runGame` completes\n- THEN `winner === 'tie'`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Game Loop\n\n### Requirement: Turn sequencing\n\nThe engine MUST follow this loop:\n\n1. Player X moves first (turn 0)\n2. After each player move, the bot moves — UNLESS the game is already over\n3. Player turns are indexed 0..4 (maximum 5 player turns)\n4. Game ends when: (a) either player achieves three-in-a-row, OR (b) the board is full\n5. `history` MUST contain one entry per move in chronological order\n6. After `runGame()` returns, NO API globals remain on `globalThis`\n\n**Maximum total moves**: 9 (5 player + 4 bot). A game MUST always terminate.\n\n#### Scenario: Player wins on turn 2\n\n- GIVEN a `playerFn` that produces a winning three-in-a-row on turn 2\n- WHEN `runGame` completes\n- THEN `winner === 'X'` AND the bot does not move after the winning player move AND `history` ends with the winning player move\n\n#### Scenario: Bot wins mid-game\n\n- GIVEN a `playerFn` that never blocks\n- WHEN the bot achieves three-in-a-row\n- THEN `winner === 'O'` AND no further player or bot moves are recorded in `history`\n\n---\n\n## 6. Module Layout\n\n### Requirement: File structure\n\nThe engine MUST be organized as:\n```\nsrc/\n  board/    — makeBoard, applyMove, legalMoves, checkWinner, isFull\n  bot/      — minimax(board, depth, isMaximizing) → { move, score }\n  api/      — buildPlayerAPI(state) → globals object; TrikiError class; error codes\n  engine/   — runGame(playerFn, options); runPlayerTurn; edge-case validators\n  index.js  — re-exports runGame only\n```\n\nThe engine MUST work as `\u003cscript type=\"module\" src=\"src/index.js\"\u003e` in a browser tab with no bundler, AND via `node --test`.\n\nA minimal `package.json` with `\"type\": \"module\"` and `\"scripts\": { \"test\": \"node --test\" }` MUST exist. Zero runtime dependencies.\n\n---\n\n## 7. Acceptance Criteria\n\n| AC | Assertion |\n|----|-----------|\n| AC-01 | `runGame(fn)` returns an object with exactly the keys `winner`, `turns`, `history`, `errors` |\n| AC-02 | `winner` is always one of `'X'`, `'O'`, `'tie'` — no other value is possible |\n| AC-03 | When `playerFn` never calls `jugar()`, `errors[0].code === 'ERR_NO_JUGAR'` AND `winner` is eventually determined (game does not hang) |\n| AC-04 | When `playerFn` calls `jugar(f,c)` twice, `errors` contains `ERR_JUGAR_TWICE` AND the first move is applied (not the second) |\n| AC-05 | When `playerFn` calls `jugar(1,1)` and the bot previously played `[1,1]`, `errors` contains `ERR_CELL_OCCUPIED` |\n| AC-06 | When `playerFn` runs an infinite loop, after `maxTurnMs` the error `ERR_INFINITE_LOOP` is logged AND the game continues |\n| AC-07 | When `playerFn` calls `jugar(-1, 0)`, `errors` contains `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` |\n| AC-08 | When `playerFn` calls `jugar(3, 3)`, `errors` contains `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` |\n| AC-09 | `última_jugada_bot()` returns `[-1,-1]` on turn 0 without throwing |\n| AC-10 | After `runGame()` returns, `globalThis.celda`, `globalThis.jugar`, `globalThis.turno`, `globalThis.mi_símbolo`, `globalThis.bot_símbolo`, `globalThis.última_jugada_bot` are all `undefined` |\n| AC-11 | Two consecutive calls to `runGame(sameFn)` produce identical `{ winner, turns, history }` (determinism) |\n| AC-12 | `history` entries are ordered chronologically; each entry has `{ turn, player, move }` |\n| AC-13 | `turno` is non-writable: `playerFn` attempting `turno = 99` does NOT change the engine's internal turn index |\n| AC-14 | Bot never loses: in 100 games against random player, `winner !== 'O'` in all 100 |\n| AC-15 | Board-full game resolves to `{ winner: 'tie' }` with no entry in `errors` |\n\n---\n\n## 8. End-to-End Scenarios\n\n#### Scenario: Center opening, game continues\n\n- GIVEN an empty board\n- WHEN `playerFn` calls `jugar(1,1)`\n- THEN bot plays a corner (priority 7 if center just taken) AND `history` has two entries (player [1,1], bot corner) AND the game has not ended\n\n#### Scenario: Player double-threat forces win\n\n- GIVEN turn 0 player plays [0,0], turn 1 player plays [1,1]\n- WHEN turn 2 player plays [2,2] (completing diagonal)\n- THEN `winner === 'X'` AND bot made 2 moves before game ended AND `turns === 5` (3 player + 2 bot)\n\n#### Scenario: Bot blocks correctly\n\n- GIVEN player has pieces at [0,0] and [0,1] (two in a row)\n- WHEN bot evaluates its move\n- THEN bot plays [0,2] (blocking) regardless of other open cells\n\n#### Scenario: No-jugar error, game continues\n\n- GIVEN `playerFn` is `() =\u003e {}` (never calls jugar)\n- WHEN `runGame` runs all 5 turns\n- THEN `errors` has 5 entries all with code `ERR_NO_JUGAR` AND `winner === 'O'` (bot wins by default after all turns lost) OR `winner === 'tie'` if board fills\n\n#### Scenario: Infinite loop cut\n\n- GIVEN `playerFn` is `() =\u003e { while(true) {} }`\n- WHEN `runGame` runs\n- THEN after `maxTurnMs` (default 100ms) the engine stops the turn AND `errors` contains `ERR_INFINITE_LOOP` AND the game continues to subsequent turns\n\n#### Scenario: Full board, forced tie\n\n- GIVEN a board state guaranteed to fill without a winner (constructed via specific `playerFn` + bot responses)\n- WHEN `runGame` completes\n- THEN `winner === 'tie'` AND `turns === 9` AND `errors` is empty\n\n#### Scenario: Unintended victory hint\n\n- GIVEN `playerFn` calls `jugar(0,0)` each turn without reading any board state\n- WHEN that move happens to complete three-in-a-row\n- THEN `winner === 'X'` AND `errors` contains one entry with code `WARN_UNINTENDED_VICTORY`\n\n#### Scenario: Globals teardown on error\n\n- GIVEN `playerFn` throws by calling `jugar(5,5)`\n- WHEN the error is caught by the engine\n- THEN after the turn, `typeof celda === 'undefined'` in the outer scope\n\n---\n\n## Risks / Spec-Level Assumptions\n\n**RISK-1 — ERR_TURN_NOT_COVERED undetectable in Fase 0**: The SDD lists it as a separate error, but raw JS cannot distinguish \"no jugar AND no structural coverage\" from \"no jugar AND bad logic\". Spec assumes Fase 0 collapses it into `ERR_NO_JUGAR`. This is a deliberate, documented downgrade — not a silent resolution.\n\n**RISK-2 — WARN_UNINTENDED_VICTORY heuristic is fuzzy**: Detecting \"active victory intention\" requires knowing which cells the player read before playing. The heuristic (no board-read before winning jugar) may produce false positives. Spec flags this as a best-effort hint in Fase 0; Fase 3 transpiler can provide full structural analysis.\n\n**RISK-3 — Proposal D5 ambiguity resolved here**: Proposal deferred \"turn-0 última_jugada_bot semantics\" to design. This spec LOCKS it: the function returns `[-1,-1]` silently; the error surfaces via `ERR_COORD_OUT_OF_RANGE` if that value is passed to `jugar()`. The `fix` field of that error MUST reference `última_jugada_bot()` behavior explicitly.\n\n**RISK-4 — Proposal D3 (global exposure shape) NOT resolved here**: Raw globals vs namespaced is an architectural decision (HOW). This spec only requires that raw globals are present during player turns. Design phase resolves namespace strategy.\n\n**RISK-5 — Proposal contradiction with SDD §6.3 speed controls**: The proposal correctly excludes `setTimeout`/speed controls from Fase 0. SDD §6.3 is a Fase 2 concern. No contradiction in scope — confirmed aligned.",
