eria`: (spec §3 row 10)\n\n- [ ] **T-031** | RED — `engine/runPlayerTurn` tests — normal flow\n  - `depends_on`: [T-026, T-027, T-028]\n  - `files`: `src/engine/runPlayerTurn.test.js`\n  - tests: `playerFn` calls `jugar(1,1)` → returns `{ pendingMove: [1,1], errors: [] }`; globals are installed before fn call and deleted after; `boardReadLog` tracks which read-globals the fn called\n  - `verification`: `node --test src/engine/runPlayerTurn.test.js` — fails\n  - `acceptance_criteria`: AC-10\n\n- [ ] **T-032** | RED — `engine/runPlayerTurn` tests — error paths\n  - `depends_on`: [T-031]\n  - `files`: `src/engine/runPlayerTurn.test.js` (extend)\n  - tests: `playerFn = () =\u003e {}` (no jugar) → `errors[0].code === 'ERR_NO_JUGAR'`, `pendingMove === null`; fn throws ReferenceError → wrapped as `ERR_UNINIT_VAR` in errors; fn exceeds `maxTurnMs` → `ERR_INFINITE_LOOP` in errors; globals absent after turn regardless of outcome\n  - `verification`: `node --test src/engine/runPlayerTurn.test.js` — fails\n  - `acceptance_criteria`: AC-03, AC-06, AC-10\n\n- [ ] **T-033** | GREEN — implement `engine/runPlayerTurn.js`\n  - `depends_on`: [T-031, T-032]\n  - `files`: `src/engine/runPlayerTurn.js`\n  - orchestrates: `buildPlayerAPI` → `installGlobals` → `try { runWithTimeout(playerFn, maxMs) } catch(e) { classify error } finally { teardownGlobals }`; post-return: if `getPendingMove() === null` push `ERR_NO_JUGAR`; merges `getErrors()` into returned array\n  - `verification`: `node --test src/engine/runPlayerTurn.test.js` — all pass\n  - `acceptance_criteria`: AC-03, AC-06, AC-10\n\n- [ ] **T-034** | RED — `engine/runGame` unit tests — return shape and termination\n  - `depends_on`: [T-033, T-017, T-030]\n  - `files`: `src/engine/runGame.test.js`\n  - tests: returns object with keys `winner`, `turns`, `history`, `errors`; `winner` ∈ `{'X','O','tie'}`; game always terminates (≤ 9 total moves); `turns` equals `history.length` (combined player + bot); no globals remain after return\n  -