n  - Handles stub throw gracefully (warns in console, does not crash page)\n\n---\n\n## Batch 1 — Board Module — COMPLETE\n\n### Board Shape Decision (ADR-B1)\n**Chosen**: 3x3 nested array `board[fila][col]` — values `''` | `'X'` | `'O'`.\nRationale: matches the design's `[[],[],[]]` notation, natural indexing by (fila, col), no conversion needed for winner-line coordinates (already `[fila, col]` pairs). Coord validation uses `Number.isInteger(n) \u0026\u0026 n \u003e= 0 \u0026\u0026 n \u003c= 2`.\n\n### Completed Tasks\n\n- [x] **T-006** | RED — `board/state.test.js`\n  - Tests: `makeBoard()` shape, fresh instances, `applyMove()` immutability, coord bounds, `cloneBoard()` deep copy\n  - RED confirmed: module not found on first run\n  - Test count: 10\n\n- [x] **T-007** | GREEN — `board/state.js`\n  - Exports: `makeBoard()`, `applyMove(board, fila, col, symbol)`, `cloneBoard(board)`\n  - `validateCoords(f, c)` internal helper throws `RangeError` with descriptive message for out-of-range coords\n  - Pure — all functions return new boards, never mutate input\n  - Verification: 10/10 GREEN ✓\n\n- [x] **T-008** | RED — `board/winner.test.js`\n  - Tests: 12 cases covering all 8 winning lines (3 rows, 3 cols, 2 diagonals), null/null for no winner, draw board\n  - Note: first draw fixture was wrong (O actually won anti-diagonal) — fixed to use a verified draw board\n  - RED confirmed on first run\n\n- [x] **T-009** | GREEN — `board/winner.js`\n  - Exports: `checkWinner(board)` → `{ winner: 'X'|'O'|null, line: [[f,c],[f,c],[f,c]]|null }`\n  - LINES constant: all 8 lines pre-computed — 3 rows, 3 cols, main diagonal, anti-diagonal\n  - Pure — reads board, never mutates\n  - Verification: 12/12 GREEN ✓\n\n- [x] **T-010** | RED — `board/legal.test.js`\n  - Tests: 11 cases — empty board returns 9 moves in row-major order, partial board, full board returns 0, move shape, isFull true/false, no mutation\n  - RED confirmed: module not found\n\n- [x] **T-011** | GREEN — `board/legal.js`\n  - Exports: `legalMoves(board)` → `[number, number][]` row-major; `isFull(board)` → boolean\n  - Pure double loop, no mutation\n  - Verification: 11/11 GREEN ✓\n\n### Files Created (Batch 1)\n\n| File | Lines | Notes |\n|------|-------|-------|\n| `src/board/state.js` | 60 | makeBoard, applyMove, cloneBoard; RangeError for invalid coords |\n| `src/board/state.test.js` | 72 | 10 tests |\n| `src/board/winner.js` | 42 | checkWinner; LINES constant; 8 lines |\n| `src/board/winner.test.js` | 87 | 12 tests; verified draw board fixture |\n| `src/board/legal.js` | 38 | legalMoves, isFull |\n| `src/board/legal.test.js` | 77 | 11 tests |\n\n### Dependency Check\n\n`rg \"from '\\.\\.(\\/api|\\/bot|\\/engine)'\" src/board/` → no output (zero upward deps) ✓\n\n### Deviations from Design\n\n1. **Draw board fixture** (T-008): First test fixture was miscounted — position set [0,2], [1,1], [2,0] for 'O' forms the anti-diagonal. Fixed with a verified draw board. Implementation correct, test corrected.\n2. **`validateCoords` in state.js only**: Tasks noted RangeError for applyMove; legal.js and winner.js do NOT validate coords (they only read boards, never take user-supplied coords). Winner checks via LINES constant (safe), legal iterates 0..2 (safe). This matches the instruction \"any function taking (fila, col)\" — winner/legal don't take coords.\n\n---\n\n## Full Suite Result (after Batch 1)\n\n`npm test` → 33 tests, 33 pass, 0 fail ✓\n\n---\n\n## Files Created (Batch 0)\n\n| File | Lines | Notes |\n|------|-------|-------|\n| `package.json` | 10 | Valid JSON, ESM, zero deps |\n| `.gitignore` | 4 | node_modules, .DS_Store, dist/, *.log |\n| `src/index.js` | 8 | VERSION + stub runGame |\n| `README.md` | 65 | Usage + limitations |\n| `index.html` | 42 | Browser smoke page |\n| `src/board/.gitkeep` | 0 | placeholder |\n| `src/bot/.gitkeep` | 0 | placeholder |\n| `src/api/.gitkeep` | 0 | placeholder |\n| `src/engine/.gitkeep` | 0 | placeholder |\n\n---\n\n## Deviations from Desig